so you've been learning a language for a  while and you've got this horrible  feeling that you're not making progress  anymore try as you might there's a  single thought you can't get out of your  head i feel stuck  if you're in the situation you might be  wondering how i can get unstuck and  start making progress again lucky for  you  i know just the solution and even better  i've got a special surprise for you that  will help you implement the solution  into your language learning so you will  never ever get stuck again just remember  to stay tuned until the very end of this  video  hi i'm luca from lucarameter.com and i'm  an italian language coach who currently  speaks 14 languages and i help people  learn languages better faster and in a  smart way so as i was saying there's one  point in the language learning journey  where even the most serious language  learners get stuck a place where despite  their best efforts progress just doesn't  seem to come as easily as it used to  this is a place most language learners  call the intermediate plateau we call it  a plateau because it's one of the first  places on your language learning journey  where progress becomes virtually flat  it's not like the beginner stages where  you're seemingly learning new things  every time you sit down to learn nor is  it like the advanced stages where  learning feels easy like you're just  filling in the gaps if you're stuck at  the intermediate plateau learning feels  difficult and slow you're not seeing  easy daily progress and you don't feel  confident enough yet to go out and make  friends read books or watch tv shows or  movies comfortably but let me quickly  teach you something that most people do  not know about the intermediate plateau  it has a lot to do with your language  learning comfort zone when you first  started learning a language everything  was fresh and everything was new because  you were learning basic words and  phrases everything felt risk-free and  relatively easy as time went on  everything that once felt new suddenly  felt comfortable you could understand a  few things say a few things usually just  enough to feel competent at the things  you wanted to do and because you felt  competent a certain range of learning  activities became your comfort zone this  is probably where you are now there's an  expression that goes what got you here  won't get you there in a language  learning context it means that to move  beyond where you are now you need to  change how you do things and to move  beyond the intermediate plateau you  specifically need to change how you go  about practicing your target language  you need to move beyond what i call  simple practice to a more challenging  type of practice called deliberate  practice  deliberate practice is a research-backed  form of skill development that involves  breaking down skills into their  essential components recognizing and  addressing your weak points and then  rebuilding that skill a new  than it was before language learning is  at its core a set of skills so if you  can learn how to break down and rebuild  your skills in this way you can learn to  stretch your capabilities beyond your  comfort zone and finally get out of the  intermediate plateau take for example my  deliberate practice based approach to  improving my speaking skills this is an  activity i only engage in when i'm  around the intermediate level usually  three to six months after i started  learning a language the first thing i do  is find a reliable native speaker that i  can regularly talk to most of the time i  use a service like itoki to hire a tutor  that i can speak to every week most  people would stop here they talk to the  tutor a couple of times a week about  anything and everything maybe get some  feedback and then  they probably never think about that  session ever again that's simple  practice which again won't get you where  you want to go to deliberately practice  my speaking skills i schedule regular  30-minute sessions with a tutor usually  once or twice a week prepare exactly  what i want to talk about before every  session including coming up with a list  of words or key phrases that i want to  use i direct the conversation towards  the topic and ideas i prepare for i ask  for specific kinds of feedback tailored  to the exact aspects of my speaking  skills that i want to improve i record  the entire session with permission of  course and save it for later reviews in  the days after the session i re-listen  to the conversation and note anything  important i want to memorize or address  in later tutoring sessions as you can  see this process is much more involved  than a typical tutoring session  but i found that it is exactly what i  and other learners need to push their  speaking skills beyond the intermediate  plateau and towards fluency and although  this is a process i designed just for  speaking the rules of deliver practice  can be applied to all of the other  language skills as well like listening  reading writing even grammar and  pronunciation if you want your language  skills to survive beyond the plateau  this is the kind of action you need to  be ready to take you need to narrow your  focus on specific skills break them down  fix them and build them back again if  you watch this far you might be saying  but luca i'm a busy person how can i do  all that all by myself when i've never  even reached fluency in a language  before  well that's why i'm here after spending  over 30 years learning languages and  more than 10 years coaching others to  learn them i visited the intermedia  plaza again and again i've learned it's  ins and outs i know where the pitfalls  lie and i've got it others safely past  them simply put as a speaker of 14  languages i can show you the way beyond  the intermediate plateau so that even if  you've ever stuck there again you'll  know just how to get unstuck and find a  way through and now for the surprise i  mentioned at the very beginning as i  said i know just the right strategies to  help you overcome the intermediate  plateau for your current target language  and any language you might learn in the  future  and i want to teach them to you not just  one or two strategies but all of them  and i plan to do that through my brand  new six week webinar course titled  overcoming the intermediate plateau this  will be a six week webinar-based course  where you will work directly with me my  team and other like-minded language  learners to help take your existing  language skills and bring them beyond  the dreaded intermediate plateau to the  point where you can use your target  language at a fluent conversational  level these are powerful methods that  will challenge your skills and give you  structure and direction at a time when  language learning progress is slow and  hardest to see if you master these  methods you will have everything you  need to finally become fluent just like  you've always dreamed of  but don't take my word for it here's  what some of my students have to say  about the very same methods you will be  learning in these webinars hi my name is  brian i am not a polyglot uh in fact  french is the first language that i've  been tackling as an adult  and i'm probably about the  a2 b1 level right now been studying for  about a year  and i want to tell you a little bit  about uh  my impressions of working with luca so  before luca i spent probably the first  eight months of this year trying a  variety of different methods  some focused on speaking right away  more grammar study based others using  prepared stories and dialogues tons of  different apps  but what i think  luca offers that's really separates  himself from the pack is  that he has a really sound understanding  of  language learning theory and then on top  of this theory he's built really  effective tools so uh his language  learning theory is distinct from some of  these other approaches and that  he understands that the research shows  the best way to learn languages is more  like how a child's orange learns  language by exposure to comprehensible  input in that in the target language um  and  this tends to work a lot better than  just learning a bunch of grammar rules  or vocab lists and then trying to apply  that knowledge  um so so that's first but then using  this theory uh he's built a bunch of  really effective practical tools that  will help you know exactly what to do  every day when you sit down to do your  language work  whether you're studying for 15 minutes a  day or an hour a day or more  and they scale really nicely from the  beginning stages all the way up to  advanced stages  and also they really allow you to use  all this amazing free content on the  internet um to to center your language  studies around uh and plus they're just  a ton of fun um so  my experience so far with luca for the  last several months has been amazing my  french has been  getting better very quickly and and i've  been having a lot of fun at it uh so  it's my opinion that if you've come  across luca's content i think you should  consider yourself really lucky and just  uh just go for it just go ahead and work  with him  so i just want to say thanks to luca for  sharing all this wonderful knowledge uh  with the rest of us  hi my name is uh george dick um a couple  of weeks ago i planted a couple of  cherry trees in our yard and later was  having a conversation with somebody  about fruit trees in general and he said  the best time to plant a fruit tree is  10 years ago the second best time is  right now  and that's really how i feel about  working with luca  i can't even imagine the kind of  progress i would have made in my last 30  years of studying languages on and off  if i had been working with luca in his  methodologies  um i really started working with luca as  a coach about a year ago i think  and um the amount of progress i've been  able to make in just a year compared to  the amount of things that i did that  weren't particularly effective over the  previous years is is just amazing  whether it's starting a language from  scratch or working up to something i'm  about to take the c1 exam um in a few  weeks for spanish finally  and i think i'm gonna pass we'll see  um but the the strategies that he has  for  getting better at speaking getting  better at writing or just just  astounding um and whatever service that  he puts together is just something i  would jump at the opportunity to work  with  um  i'm so glad that i found luca when i did  and i hope that you  take advantage of his methods sooner  rather than later because you just will  be thrilled with the impact that he's  able to have on your  language learning adventures  thanks a lot bye-bye  these words fill me with joy they're  proof that when you're armed with the  right mindset and the right tools  anything is possible that's why i'm so  excited to release this live course i  can finally share my intermediate level  language learning techniques and  strategies with many more people than i  could ever do in a one-on-one coaching  session  and if you think each of these webinars  sounds exciting wait until you hear  about all the extras you will be  receiving as well beyond the six two  hour webinars of the course in fact you  will receive access to our two weekly  one-hour group calls with me to ask  questions and share your progress access  to our learner community and circle so  you can interact with dedicated learners  just like you weekly missions along with  pdf guides that will teach you how to  tailor the course techniques to specific  languages monthly q a sessions with me  and by team and so much more  best of all if you join the six week  course you'll automatically gain access  to our video based online version of the  same course when we release it next year  so what do you think you now know  everything you need to know about my  brand new overcoming the intermediate  plateau live course are you finally  ready to conquer the intermediate  plateau and reach the fluency you have  always wanted there will be only 100  seats available for this webinar series  and that will be filled on a first come  first served basis without exception so  if you're interested please check and  click the link on the description box  below to learn more about how you can  sign up i cannot wait to see you in the  course  happy language learning and talk to you  soon  [Music]  you

